WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.033
Thermal imaging senses infrared radiation and displays apparent temperature patterns.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:09.473
It does not reveal hidden truth, identify exact causes,

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:12.433
or operate like a visible-light photograph.

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:17.860
Useful work depends on sensor type, resolution, sensitivity, lens, calibration context,

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.313
distance, angle, target size, and environmental conditions.

00:00:21.313 --> 00:00:24.767
Time, sun, wind, moisture, material, reflections, geometry,

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:28.713
and recent operating history can change the scene.

00:00:28.713 --> 00:00:34.633
Plan collection around a defined question, authorized area, useful contrast, stable coverage,

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.113
safety, and privacy.

00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:40.553
Preserve original data, metadata, settings, conditions, and source links.

00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:44.500
Interpret patterns against appropriate backgrounds and comparable components.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.460
Separate observation, anomaly judgment, and diagnosis.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.420
Use calibrated confidence, identify alternative causes,

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.873
and seek domain-specialist review for consequential findings.

00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:56.833
The goal is useful, defensible observation,

00:00:56.833 --> 00:01:00.780
not unsupported conclusions from colors on a screen.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:05.713
Strong thermal work combines planning, sensor awareness, environmental context, documentation,

00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:08.180
cautious reporting, and responsible use.
